            "review_title": "Review at Kieu Bao Barbecue",
            "review_text": "Manuel D\n120 contributions\n0\nTry it\nNov 2025 • Family\nWe found this place on Google looking for foodplaces to be in the City. We almost passed the Shop since downstairs looks more like a garage for motorbikes than a Restaurant.\n\nAt a very small counter you order your mal which is either grillen pork, minced pork or springrolls in a combination with glass noodles and greens. You can also mix it for a combination of All 3 Extras. If you wish for more noodles additions are free.\n\nAfter your order you can go upstairs, take a seat and wait for your order to arrive. The dining area is very minimalistic which gives the place a unique feel. The food is what it is all about. A whole 2 liter Bucket of \"nuoc mam\" the local fish sauce makes the dish. Its fresh, its well made and screams \"umami\".\n\nWe enjoyed it a lot.\nRead more\nWritten December 1, 2025",
